+#### Max Consecutive Losses
+
+`MaxConsecutiveLosses` looks at the most recent trades within `lookback_period` in minutes (or in candles when using `lookback_period_candles`), for a single pair as well as across all pairs.
+If the last `trade_limit` trades in a row all resulted in a loss (a trade counts as a loss when its profit is below `required_profit`), that pair will be locked for `stop_duration` in minutes (or in candles when using `stop_duration_candles`, or until the set time when using `unlock_at`) - and, unless `only_per_pair` is set to true, trading will also stop for all pairs, since a losing streak like this often signals that current market conditions aren't a good fit for the strategy in general, not just for a single pair.
+
+Any winning trade (profit >= `required_profit`) resets the streak.
+
+Make sure `lookback_period` (or `lookback_period_candles`) is wide enough to actually contain `trade_limit` trades for your strategy and timeframe - if fewer trades than `trade_limit` fall within the window, the protection cannot trigger.
+
+The below example locks a pair (and, since `only_per_pair` is not set, the whole bot) for 4 hours after 4 consecutive losing trades within the last 2 days.
+
+``` python
+@property
+def protections(self):
+    return [
+        {
+            "method": "MaxConsecutiveLosses",
+            "lookback_period_candles": 48,
+            "trade_limit": 4,
+            "stop_duration_candles": 4,
+            "required_profit": 0.0,
+            "only_per_pair": False,
+        }
+    ]
+```
+
+Setting `only_per_pair` to `true` will restrict this protection to individual pairs only, without ever locking trading bot-wide.
+
 ### Full example of Protections
 
 All protections can be combined at will, also with different parameters, creating a increasing wall for under-performing pairs.
